   "etymology": "Doublet of thep, with affricated initial consonant. More at thep.\nPart of a rich phonolexical series represented by variants covering almost all vocalic grades (\"a\", \"e\", \"i\", \"o\", \"u\") and with consonantal variants with \"c\", \"ç\", \"q\", and \"sh\" (çak, cek, çek, qek, cik, çik, cok, çok, qok, cuk, quk, çuk, etc).\nSource of Romanian țeapă, or cognate to it from a common pre-Roman term of Balkan substratum. Possible co-source of Romanian țipilic (“peak, top”) and țăpălic (“id.”).",
   "etymology_class": null,
   "source_lang": null,
   "cognate": null,
